  {
    "episode_id": 80104,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80104.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "And I wonder, you spoke a lot there about liability around the internet. And we had Kent Walker from Google on the podcast, and I asked him if he essentially thought that those internet protections should be extended or as written or extended into AI and companies sort of responsibility for how their AI models are used by third parties. His answer was not no. His answer was not that they're not protected. I think tech companies will probably look at ways to protect themselves and their AI models. So is that an area where you think Congress should focus as sort of the liability for AI, finding ways that tech companies are held more liable for how these new models are utilized.",
